course: dictionary
lesson: 13986
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, tell you which meaning is right. «The two friends were at loggerheads over which film to watch.» The clue is the argument, so at loggerheads means they strongly disagreed. It is not about anything to do with heads.
explain: A word can also name a living thing. «The loggerheads swam back out to sea after dark.» Here loggerheads are animals, large sea turtles with big heads. Ask yourself: does this word fit the sentence as a thing, or as a feeling of argument?
explain: Some words are old and rarely used now. Long ago, loggerhead was an old word for a stupid person. If you find it in an old book, check the sentence and a dictionary to be sure.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «At loggerheads» means disagreeing strongly and arguing with someone.
fact: A «loggerhead turtle» is a large sea turtle with a big head.
fact: «Loggerhead» was an old word for a stupid person.
fact: Loggerhead turtles lay their eggs on beaches, and they are protected.
exercise: «The two neighbours were at loggerheads about the fence.» What does at loggerheads mean? | They were fast asleep | They were lost in the garden | They were building the fence together happily | *They strongly disagreed and argued
exercise: «A loggerhead turtle laid her eggs on the beach.» What kind of thing is a loggerhead here? | A stupid person | A kind of boat | *A large sea turtle | A rock on the beach
exercise: «The loggerheads swam back out to sea after dark.» What does loggerheads mean here? | *Large sea turtles | Two people arguing | A kind of seaweed | Stupid people
test: «The chess players were at loggerheads, and neither would give in.» What does at loggerheads mean? | *They were arguing strongly | They were very tired | They were playing happily together | They were sleeping
test: In «The loggerhead nested on the sand», which meaning fits best? | Two people who disagree | A type of tree | *A large sea turtle | A stupid person
exam: Ella reads «Mum and Dad are at loggerheads about the holiday.» What does Ella work out? | Mum has gone to sleep | *They strongly disagree and argue about it | They are both lost | Dad is at the beach with a turtle
